; The PM51 board demo: music and graphics from a PureMetal program compiled by
; PureMetal Forge's 8051 target. GENERATED by demo/make_demo.py from
; demo/pm51_demo.template (the tables); edit the template.
;
; The board (README, "The PM51 display board"): bitmap $8000, text $D000,
; text colour $D200, sprites $D400, sprite patterns $D800, line colours $DC00,
; I/O $F000. Everything is polled: the 8051 target has no interrupt handlers.
EnableExplicit

Global frame.w, steps.w, tick.w, i.w, x.w, y.w, c.w, v.w, a.w, k.w
Global buttons.w, lastButtons.w, direction.w, muted.w, scroll.w, scrollPos.w
Global leadVol.w, bassVol.w, drumVol.w, drumKind.w, textColour.w
; The tables, in XDATA RAM (written by InitTables): notes as MIDI numbers
; (0 hold, 1 rest), a frequency for each MIDI note, drums, colours, the message.
#T_LEAD = $E000
#T_BASS = $E040
#T_DRUM = $E080
#T_FREQ = $E100
#T_RAINBOW = $E200
#T_MSG = $E300
Dim bx.w[8]
Dim by.w[8]
Dim bdx.w[8]
Dim bdy.w[8]

